body:
I think your approach here makes sense. Before init, sendEvent means nothing.
I'm just reminded that I should change my previous implementations to this.

What I did before is to assign them inside getWidgetRenderState:

```js
getWidgetRenderState() {
  if (!sendEvent) {
    sendEvent = ...
  }

  return {
    ...
  }
}
```

We just need to make sure when we tests the return of `getWidgetRenderState` **BEFORE** init will have undefined sendEvent.

